{%- comment -%}
  App EMBED. This is the one that matters commercially.

  Shopify will not let a public app write theme files at all — themeFilesUpsert
  needs an exemption we do not have — so the app cannot switch on the theme's own
  pickup block for the merchant. And themes disagree about that block: Dawn
  renders pickup unconditionally, Horizon ships with show_pickup_availability
  set to false, so a brand new Horizon store has pickup working perfectly at
  checkout and every product page silent about it. Verified on a live storefront:
  the product page said nothing at all.

  Sending the merchant into the theme editor to find a setting they have never
  heard of is exactly the step that loses them. An app embed is the one thing
  Shopify does allow: the merchant enables it once, from a deep link inside our
  app, and it then renders on every product page of any theme without a template
  being edited.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if product -%}
  <div
    class="miko-cc-embed"
    data-miko-cc-embed
    data-position="{{ block.settings.position }}"
    style="--miko-cc-accent: {{ block.settings.accent }};"
    hidden
  >
    {% render 'miko-pickup', product: product %}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Click & Collect pickup",
  "target": "body",
  "stylesheet": "miko-pickup.css",
  "javascript": "miko-pickup.js",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "position",
      "label": "Where to show it",
      "options": [
        { "value": "after_buy", "label": "Under the Add to cart button" },
        { "value": "before_buy", "label": "Above the Add to cart button" }
      ],
      "default": "after_buy"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "accent",
      "label": "Accent colour",
      "default": "#1a7f4b"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
